# C3 R2 broad boundary result

**BOUNDARY_DIFFERENTIAL over captured states; R3 remains pending lifetime and negative-test gates.** Source base `9e9ea16`; target artifact SHA-256 `582bd40f6886200101f4c4ed9f25f3fe80cc14c86e9e2b37746cd8904a0c622d`; streamed backend SHA `1248fd8fa8cfebaece5ea992e4d951c1e18bb9d5`. Token IDs SHA-256 `8fb3aff447febaeaa5a8bdd0c485fd20d51d39fb6ac3e6ba4849eb4a664dbc23`. Target capture binary SHA-256 `d451271d19bd25371fd5a9966f3412ea042790fc3f1509b546530c54edcdfec8`; corrected reference binary SHA-256 `dce4ba6b59c2a34af3e4c5296c0b14e21719dbb00b1b07c0bcf416b31eebfab2`.

| Case | Target capture | Canonical layer replay | Direct consumed bytes |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| `log_medium`, 189+43 IDs | 36 layers, 7 selected FFN invocations/layer, 3,689 tensors/84,548,464 B captured | 252/252 routing IDs, weights and final FFN outputs bitwise equal | 468/468 active slices equal, 1,033,793,280 B |
| `spec_pressure`, 414+49 IDs | 36 layers, 7 invocations/layer, 3,689 tensors/85,419,264 B captured | 252/252 bitwise equal | 480/480 active slices equal, 1,060,300,800 B |

Each replay reconstructs one full canonical 128-expert layer at a time from GGUF offsets, releases it, then advances. The replay graph contains the native router, `MUL_MAT_ID`, `ADD_ID`, GPT-OSS SwiGLU, masking-independent expert outputs and weighted reduction. It uses the captured real normalized FFN input, shape and token IDs; no streamed cache or physical slot remap. All 504 comparisons include three prefill microbatches (starts 0, 128 and last 32-aligned prompt chunk) and decode continuation positions 0/1/7/31. The actual per-layer token counts are in the compact JSON summaries, not assumed from configured context. CPU layers 0–28 and GPU layers 29–35 were replayed on their true production devices. No numerical tolerance was used. This is conditional on the captured upstream activation and cannot certify attention/KV or arbitrary prompts.

The direct byte checker read canonical encoded slices independently and compared the actual three MXFP4 matrix slices addressed by physical slot IDs and three F32 bias slices addressed by logical expert IDs. It covered active pairs only in layer 0 and layer 35 at `prefill0`/`decode0`; other layers have only the independent FFN differential. CPU layer 0 used multiple nonempty waves and physically reused slots for different logical experts in both cases (30 slots in `log_medium`, 31 in `spec_pressure` observed in the ledger). The ledger proves correct bytes at those consumer points; it does not yet record `slot_gen`, in-flight eviction or failure behavior. Ready-hit/cold/reload classes cannot be assigned from the current compact ledger alone.

The two captures completed under memory.max18 GiB/swap.max0 with zero OOM/max/kill and zero runtime swap. Cgroup memory peaks: 14,892,269,568 B (`log`) and 14,834,663,424 B (`spec`); sampled GPU peak 3904 MiB in both. Max observed CPU/NVMe were 88.625/48.85 C and 89.625/54.85 C; GPU sample peak 58 C. Capture times 73.732/140.599 s include callbacks and are **not** production prefill timing. Raw capture indices SHA-256: `8f4283bfa034b7a4a23cc16991b89325304dcb3caa19b2f5c4594d98df71ad0b` and `4054d80fd7a46635c90e4bc6d22f1290e57f95bf37e9381931021ed2b1789704`. Byte ledgers SHA-256: `4e4d70aaafba68e9b460f7b521b139ad5ac9207ad0e18c102bc41e61db26d845` and `e5e65e642759876ed2c2e6fd8940b8165abe0a23e43e45ffb71726a70f2f39e9`.

The first all-layer reference attempt stopped at layer 28 and remains FAIL. It wrongly treated `-ngl 8` as eight MoE layers on GPU; the loader offloads the output layer and seven MoE layers. Its mismatch is preserved in `results/c3-r2-broad-log-reference-summary01.json`. The placement correction and fresh `-02` identities are documented in `C3-R2-BROAD-REFERENCE-REPAIR-20260926.md`. The successful summaries are `results/c3-r2-broad-log-reference-summary02.json` and `results/c3-r2-broad-spec-reference-summary02.json`; per-layer manifests and raw arrays remain local. No C1/C2 result was changed.

Remaining gates: exact slot generations/in-flight lifetime, deliberate negative mutants, target EIO/EOF/short/delayed read tests, and broader callback OFF/ON parity. The earlier OFF/ON comparison covers two full-logit positions only. P1/P2 prefill optimization has not begun.
